From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: playportdev <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:38:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: replay early images after the emulator starts

PLA-476: kernel32 is loaded as an emulator dependency before the
image-notification exports or executable tracker exist. The game's stock
helper calls its LoadLibraryExW x64 stub from chrome_elf TLS
initialization; with no tracked interval FEX emits NOEXEC and its
deliberate NULL-read trampoline, not a genuine NULL dereference in
chrome_elf. Replay the loader list through the existing guarded
intervals-only entry after successful ProcessInit/ThreadInit and before
guest callbacks. The loader lock pins every image; duplicate section
inserts are idempotent. Do not replay ImageTracker or map side effects,
and do not change retained-slot ownership or parked threads.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-29-sc-stock-cef-probe.md
Offered-upstream: no; iOS pseudo-process notification gap
---
 dlls/ntdll/loader.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
index a99c46f..538b362 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
@@ -6020,6 +6020,23 @@ static void load_arm64ec_module(void)
         NtTerminateProcess( GetCurrentProcess(), status );
     }
     ERR( "load_arm64ec_module: arm64ec_process_init returned cleanly, status=%lx\n", status );
+
+    /* PLA-476: the emulator's dependencies were mapped before its notification
+     * exports and trackers existed. Replay them now, before guest TLS callbacks.
+     * loader_section is held, so the list and images stay alive. Use only the
+     * guarded, intervals-only API: the full map callback takes FEX's code lock
+     * exclusively and is not safe under the loader lock. Duplicate executable
+     * section inserts (main image, ntdll, queued maps) are harmless. */
+    {
+        LIST_ENTRY *list = &NtCurrentTeb()->Peb->LdrData->InLoadOrderModuleList;
+        LIST_ENTRY *entry;
+
+        for (entry = list->Flink; entry != list; entry = entry->Flink)
+        {
+            LDR_DATA_TABLE_ENTRY *mod = CONTAINING_RECORD( entry, LDR_DATA_TABLE_ENTRY, InLoadOrderLinks );
+            arm64ec_notify_image_map( mod->DllBase );
+        }
+    }
 }

 #endif
